# The desktop's Print of SET128.TXT, every Atari character from 128 to 255
# (tools/dev/st/make_set128.py): what a program that sends a file's bytes as
# they are gives the printer for the characters above ASCII. As print-desktop,
# on a launcher with SET128.TXT where print-desktop's has PRINT.TXT (the same
# place in the window).
@printer
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/launchers/desktop-set128.st
wait 100
key 0x01
desktop 2500
wait 50
mouse 280 180
click left 2
wait 25
mouse 180 51
click left 2
wait 25
mouse 88 5
mouse 88 14
click left 2
wait 100
printwatch
mouse 160 127
click left 2
printer 100 3000
